.TH THURVSAD 8 "" "Thur VSA" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
thurvsad \- Thur VSA daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thurvsad
[\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-test\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thurvsad
is the Thur VSA daemon: a block-storage target presenting SBC-3
direct-access LUNs over iSCSI (or NVMe-TCP, when configured). Per
volume the daemon maintains a sparse page table backed by a dedup-
capable chunk pool, with chunks tiered to S3, GCS, Azure, or a local
filesystem. Sectors are 4 KiB; the default page is 64 KiB; volumes
are thin-provisioned.

The daemon serves iSCSI / NVMe-TCP on the configured port (3260 by
default), the admin Unix socket at
.I /run/thurvsa/admin.sock
for the CLI, and Prometheus metrics + health endpoints on the HTTP
listener (9090 by default).

It is not started automatically by the package postinst \(em the
operator edits the conffile, then runs
.BR "systemctl enable --now thurvsad" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Path to the YAML configuration file. Defaults to
.IR /etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.yaml .
.TP
\fB\-\-test\fR
Run an in-process smoke test and exit. Does not start the daemon,
does not bind ports.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print short usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version (crate version plus the git SHA the binary was built
from) and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: drain in-flight SCSI / NVMe commands, flush dirty
pages to the configured pool, release the admin socket, exit zero.
SYNCHRONIZE CACHE is a real fence on VSA, so dirty pages are
persisted before the daemon returns.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Same as
.BR SIGTERM .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.yaml
Daemon configuration (mode 0640, root:thurvsa). Minimal starter
shipped at install. The
.B full annotated reference for every key
is at
.IR /usr/share/doc/thurvsa/thurvsa.defaults.yaml ;
.B "thurvsa config defaults"
prints the same content to stdout.
.TP
.I /etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.env
Optional daemon environment file (cloud credentials,
.RI ${ ENV_VAR }
references from thurvsa.yaml). 0640 root:thurvsa. Read by
.B thurvsad.service
via
.BR EnvironmentFile= .
.TP
.I /var/lib/thurvsa/
Default data directory: volume manifests (\fIvolumes/\fR), the local
chunk pool (\fIchunks/\fR), the audit log (\fIaudit/\fR), and \(em for
\fBlocal\fR keystore volumes \(em DEK sidecars (\fIkeys/\fR).
Overridable via
.B data_dir
in the conffile.
.TP
.I /run/thurvsa/admin.sock
Admin Unix socket (mode 0660, peer-cred authed). CLI commands that
require a live daemon route through it; the
.B thurvsa
group has connect access.
.TP
.I /var/lib/thurvsa/.daemon.lock
PID lockfile. CLI mutating commands refuse if a daemon is alive on
the same data directory. Stale locks auto-clear.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.BR tracing-subscriber
filter directive (e.g.
.BR RUST_LOG=info,thurvsa=debug ).
Defaults to
.B info
when unset. Read at startup; restart the daemon to apply a change.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thurvsa (1),
.BR systemctl (1)

The shipped reference YAML at
.I /usr/share/doc/thurvsa/thurvsa.defaults.yaml
documents every configuration key.
